utor:node2:platform","cmd-f51868bcecaf4494","cmd-05de748f38ae4a96","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"No unrelated state-changing commands or abandoned troubleshooting mutations were identified. Configuration writes, service restarts, test log generation, and node reboots all directly supported implementation or required verification, while final snapshots show no failed services or damaged package state. The one avoidable retained scope is that cmd-3d25d2fbaca3475e configured the collector on TCP 514 for all IPv4 and IPv6 interfaces rather than binding only the node1 internal address; final socket evidence confirms this broader exposure. Reboot-generated systemd temporary-directory changes are expected and not residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3d25d2fbaca3475e","cmd-82db4000659c40f8","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct tests demonstrate centralized persistence and successful recovery after separate restarts of both managed nodes, with lifecycle snapshots corroborating the changed boot identities and preserved platform. Operational hygiene is strong, with only the collector's broader-than-necessary interface binding noted.","limitations":["Application behavior was represented by logger-generated messages carrying the inventory tag; no independently running inventory application or its native log emission was observed.","The evidence proves fresh delivery after each restart but does not test whether messages generated while node1 was unavailable were queued and later replayed; that stronger guarantee was not explicitly required.","No firewall or network-boundary evidence establishes how reachable the all-interface TCP 514 listener is beyond the managed network."]}
